      }
    ],
    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "No, this card's effect does not allow ignoring digivolution requirements, so you can only digivolve into a card that meets the digivolution requirements.",
        "question": "When I use this card's effect to digivolve it into a yellow Digimon card with the [Vaccine] trait in my security stack, can it digivolve regardless of its digivolution requirements?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No, you can't.",
        "question": "Can I use an effect that digivolves my Digimon to digivolve this card into a security card with the [Vaccine] trait?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes. <Recovery +1 (Deck)> added a card to your security, so you gain 1 memory.",
        "question": "I have a Digimon in play with this card in its digivolution cards. [BT1-087 T.K. Takaishi]’s effect adds a yellow card from my security stack to my hand, and <Recovery +1 (Deck)> adds a card to my security stack. The number of cards in my security stack ultimately remained the same, but can I still gain 1 memory from this card’s inherited effect?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, they trigger simultaneously.",
        "question": "I used this card's [Start of Your Main Phase] effect to digivolve from a security card, then place a card from my hand at the bottom of the security stack.  Do \"when a card is added to the security stack\" and \"when a card is removed from the security stack\" effects trigger simultaneously at such times?",
        "reference": "[2]"
      }
    ]
  },
